// A LOCAL that shares a module `static`'s name is still a local, and its place still dangles (KR-66).
//
// The sibling of tests/reffn_static.kama, and the reason the static-storage rule resolves the root as a
// SYMBOL rather than matching a bare name: a name-only test would see `g`, find the static, and let a
// pointer to a dead frame escape — turning a widened rule into a memory-safety hole. (Whether a local may
// shadow a static at all is KR-57's question; this must be refused either way.)
static int32 g;

fn ref int32 shadow() { int32 g = 5; return g; }

fn int32 main() { return shadow(); }
